{
  "unit": {
    "id": "10",
    "title": "What used to happen",
    "blurb": "The imperfect: used to, was doing",
    "intro": "The imperfect tense describes what used to happen or was going on: -bam, -bās, -bat, -bāmus, -bātis, -bant (_amābam_, _habēbam_) or -ēbam, -ēbās… for -ere and -īre verbs (_edēbam_, _audiēbam_). Use it for habits (_cotīdiē_ = every day, _saepe_ = often) and for scenes you are describing: _puer pānem edēbat_ (the boy was eating bread). Use the perfect for a single finished event, the imperfect for a background or a habit."
  },
